This is the RAMSES parameter file for a test that combines a turbulent initial
velocity field with driving. It is the only test where initial_turb and turb are
both on, so it covers the interaction between the two: the initial field is an
independent draw, and the driving must be unaffected by it.

The box starts as broadband turbulence (power_law) and is then pushed by a
steady, fixed forcing acting on the single mode k=(1,0,0) ('test'). This covers
the two spectra being different, and the 'test' spectrum branch.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=6
levelmax=6
ngridmax=500000
boxlen=4
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.666667
courant_factor=0.8
scheme='muscl'
slope_type=1
riemann='hllc'
pressure_fix=.true.
beta_fix=0.5
/

&INIT_PARAMS
nregion=1
region_type='square'
x_center=2
y_center=2
z_center=2
length_x=4
length_y=4
length_z=4
exp_region=10
d_region=0.28954719470909174
p_region=0.030361026190591216
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=1
tout=0.25
/

&UNITS_PARAMS
units_density=1.50492957435d-20
units_time=3.1556926d13
units_length=3.0857d18
/

&COOLING_PARAMS
barotropic_eos=.true.
barotropic_eos_form='isothermal'
T_eos=4.2194
/

&TURB_PARAMS
turb=.true.
turb_type=2         ! 2=forced fixed: a steady push on one mode
turb_seed=843       ! -1 = random
comp_frac=1.0       ! fully compressive: the push is along k, i.e. along x
instant_turb=.false.
forcing_power_spectrum='test' !power_law, parabolic, konstandin, test
turb_T=0.25
turb_Ndt=100       ! Number of timesteps per autocorr. time
turb_rms=3         ! rms turbulent forcing acceleration
turb_min_rho=1d-6  ! Minimum density for turbulence
!-------------------
initial_turb=.true.
initial_turb_spectrum='power_law' ! broadband, unlike the single-mode driving
initial_turb_comp_frac=0.5        ! mixed, unlike the fully compressive driving
! Initial velocity dispersion |v|_rms. The sound speed is
! sqrt(p_region/d_region) = 0.324, so the box starts at Mach ~1.5.
initial_turb_vrms=0.5
/
